---
source: crates/sluice-cli/tests/it/help.rs
expression: "help(&[\"pair\", \"--help\"])"
---
Pair a device with a running daemon, redeem a ticket, or list the daemons this device paired with

Without `--redeem` or `--list`, the daemon makes one ticket for one device and one grant. The ticket is a secret: give it to the device, which redeems it once before it expires. `--redeem` runs on that device, and keeps the daemon under a name here.

Usage: sluice pair [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --grant <GRANT>
          The grant the ticket gives

          Possible values:
          - deliver: Hand the daemon content for its inbox, and nothing else
          - control: Every call of the control interface. Reserved for 1.2, and refused today
          
          [default: deliver]

      --json
          Print JSON, one object per line, instead of text. A failure is then a JSON line on stderr

      --color <WHEN>
          When to colour help, errors and other output. NO_COLOR set to anything turns it off

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colour a stream only when it is a terminal
          - always: Colour always, unless `NO_COLOR` is set
          - never:  Never colour
          
          [default: auto]

      --ttl <SECONDS>
          How long the ticket works, in seconds; the default is 10 minutes and the most is one hour

      --name <NAME>
          A name. For a ticket, the label the daemon writes for the device that redeems it; for a redemption, what this device calls the daemon; for a rename, the new label

      --redeem <TICKET>
          Redeem this ticket from the daemon that printed it

      --list
          Show the daemons this device has paired with, and what they granted

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
